    "summary": "Both findings fixed. (1) isUnitArtifactPath now accepts only a path already in normal form: posix.normalize(path) must equal the path and no segment may be empty, '.' or '..' (plus the existing absolute, drive-letter and backslash refusals), so 'docs/epics/<item>/./S001/LLD.md', '<item>//S001/LLD.md' and '.insrc/artifacts/./<id>.json' are refused; the checkpoint test lists those four forms for both the run and the draft variant, and the draft variant now also has its own kind, storyId-mismatch, epic-vs-story and empty-field cases. (2) inferStageWorkflow now counts an artifact only when it is committed at HEAD (git cat-file -e HEAD:<relative path> through runGit), so a draft that exists only in the working tree is not a completed stage. The named test runs in a real temporary git repository: an HLD present but uncommitted still gives design.epic, committing it gives complete; a committed LLD gives plan; an uncommitted PLAN still gives plan; committing it gives complete; an Epic being complete does not complete a Story. Everything else is as submitted; the handoff-pure test (3 tests) passes and tsc is clean.",
